commit 06cd7860c2a6f9bd6e26a4723c03a1c8c7e0052d
Author: Alain Volmat <alain.volmat@foss.st.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 15 21:01:50 2024 +0100

    pipeline: dcmipp: fix buffer number handling

    The pipeline handler was wrongly taking the assumption that the
    bufferCount provided within generateConfiguration would also be
    given into the configure functiobn. The application can ask for
    another number of buffers.
    Update the handling in order to not take the hardcoded value but
    instead the bufferCount provided via the configure function.

    Since the IPA bufferCount is also based on the V4L2 bufferCount,
    update that part as well in order to reuse the V4L2 bufferCount
    incremented by 1 to allocate IPA (params & stats) buffers.

    Signed-off-by: Alain Volmat <alain.volmat@foss.st.com>

commit f9b87283f3931cf8a81cc81a2c65fe2da25c7106
Author: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 29 17:26:56 2024 +0100

    ipa: dcmipp: increase AEC algo cycle at startup

    At startup the sensor response time may be greater than expected
    (e.g. 4 instead of 3 for IMX335). During this phase it is critical
    to provide the algorithm with the correct statistic update.
    Waiting for an additional frame during the very first frames ensures
    that the algorithm works fine.

    Signed-off-by: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>

commit cc70540add9aae3efd0bfdfbf1eb7fcc1bfa3c5c
Author: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 28 15:53:56 2024 +0100

    ipa: add sensor delay in imx335.yaml

    Add the measured sensor delay of IMX335 which is 3.
    3 is the sum of "2" (sensor delay) + "1" ISP stat report


    Signed-off-by: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>

commit 9343848d62688756c2bfad0123f0dffb3a3d6683
Author: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 30 16:45:40 2024 +0100

    gstreamer: add the sensor-delay properties

    The 'sensor-delay' property controls the sensor delay used by AEC.
    The 'do-sensor-delay-measure' property is used to start the measure.
    The 'sensor-delay-measure' property holds the reported measure.


    Signed-off-by: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>

commit d3b43cf7086366135f3afe8953203a0e9a4f770c
Author: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 30 16:31:47 2024 +0100

    ipa: dcmipp: support sensor delay measure

    When the algorithm receives the "DoSensorDelayMeasure" request, it
    applies different sensor config, and measure the number of VSYNC
    it takes before the luminance is actually updated.

    At then end it reports the measured sensor delay.

    During the measure the nominal AEC algo processing is skipped.


    Signed-off-by: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>

commit 632de6fe67bbf732e254a46f0489c10b64eb0ad5
Author: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 28 15:51:29 2024 +0100

    ipa: dcmipp: support sensor delay as an IPA parameter

    Since the sensor delay depends on the sensor, and considering that
    this value is not reported by the kernel, handle this as an IPA param.
    The AEC algorithm takes this parameter under consideration, waiting
    for the right number of frames after a sensor control update, before
    processing its algorithm.

    Review the definition of ispStatLatency (not need for 1 extra VSYNC
    because of shadow register), and update AWB accordingly.


    Signed-off-by: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>

commit 5a02003a770f2c268f010e682fce60cf5d8f99f9
Author: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 30 16:40:59 2024 +0100

    libcamera: controls: add draft sensor delay controls

    The SensorDelay control defines the delay (in number of VSYNC) between
    the time a sensor control (gain or exposure) is updated, and the time
    the frame is actually updated.

    The 'DoSensorDelayMeasure' control triggers the self measurement
    of the sensor delay.

    The 'SensorDelayMeasure' control reports the measure delay.

    These controls are expected to be used by the STM32 DCMIPP IPA to
    control the AEC behavior.


    Signed-off-by: Fabien Dessenne <fabien.dessenne@st.com>

commit 6241ed4d9af6707e8305af94d33d6a5754362b4e
